# Pisigo (https://pisigo.com)

Author: Ventsislav Arnaudov (https://varnaudov.com). Module: `github.com/arnaudovproject/pisigo`.

## Mental model

Pisigo = small HTTP core + optional packages. Prefer framework helpers over reinventing routing, errors, binding, middleware, health, or adapters.

- Boot: `app := pisigo.Boot()`
- Handlers: `func(c *pisigo.Context) error`
- Middleware: `func(next pisigo.HandlerFunc) pisigo.HandlerFunc` via `app.Use(...)` or `app.Group(prefix, mw...)`
- Return `*pisigo.HTTPError` / sentinels (`ErrNotFound`, `ErrUnauthorized`, …). Do not write status ad-hoc unless using response helpers.
- Groups join paths safely: `Group("/api")` + `GET("/users")` or `GET("users")` both work.

## Default stack

```go
app.Use(middleware.Recover(), middleware.RequestID(), middleware.Logger(), middleware.Secure())
```

Add only what the feature needs: `CORS`, `Timeout`, `RateLimit`, `CSRF`, `Compress`, `Cache`, `auth.JWT`, `session.Middleware`.

## Package map (import what you need)

| Need | Package |
|------|---------|
| HTTP core | `pisigo` |
| Middleware | `pisigo/middleware` |
| JWT / API key / roles | `pisigo/auth` |
| Cookie sessions | `pisigo/session` |
| Env/JSON config | `pisigo/config` |
| SQL | `pisigo/db` + `adapters/postgres|mysql|sqlite|mssql` |
| Mongo | `adapters/mongodb` |
| Cache/KV | `store` + `adapters/memory|redis` |
| Jobs | `queue` + `adapters/memory|redis|nats` |
| Messaging | `pubsub` + `adapters/memory|nats` |
| Migrations | `pisigo/migrate` |
| Health | `pisigo/health` |
| Prometheus | `pisigo/metrics` |
| OTel | `pisigo/otelx` |
| OpenAPI | `pisigo/openapi` |
| WS / SSE | `pisigo/websocket`, `pisigo/sse` |
| Resilience | `pisigo/circuit` |
| i18n | `pisigo/i18n` |
| Tests | `pisigo/testing` (`pisigotest`) |

## Agent rules of work

1. Reuse Pisigo APIs before adding third-party HTTP kits.
2. Keep handlers thin; put domain logic in packages (`internal/...`).
3. Prefer `c.Bind(&in)` + validate tags over manual decode.
4. Wire adapters behind interfaces (`store.Store`, `queue.Queue`, `pubsub.PubSub`, `db.SQL`).
5. Register health/metrics/openapi in `main` or `cmd/` only.
6. After changes: `go test ./...` (and race in CI).
7. English for code comments and public docs.

CLI: `pisigo new|dev|prod|generate|migrate|install agents`.

After scaffolding an app, run `pisigo install agents all` in the app root so Cursor/Claude/Codex get Pisigo-aware rules.
